                <pb facs="0622" n="498" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg498"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/3224: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Crane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-01-29T19:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 29,
                                1921—7 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 29—3:18
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>67. Your 44, January 27, 3 [<hi rendition="#italic">7</hi>] p.m. In view of
                    collective action consular body Canton described my 59, January 26, 11 a.m.,
                    Legation is calling attention consul Canton to Legation’s September 5, 8 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">7</hi>] p.m., 1918, as indicating Department’s general
                    attitude but not for further individual action by him pending Department’s
                    additional instructions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Crane</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
